lwIP for QEMU
=============

This directory holds the parts of lwIP (https://savannah.nongnu.org/projects/lwip/)
that QEMU uses, unchanged, from the release tag STABLE-2_2_1_RELEASE
(commit 77dcd25a72509eb83f72b033d219b1d40cd8eb95):

  COPYING, README                 the licence (BSD-3-Clause) and the upstream README
  src/core/*.c, src/core/ipv4/*.c the core, IPv4, ARP, ICMP, IP fragmentation, raw, UDP, TCP
                                  (without ACD, AutoIP, DHCP, IGMP, DNS, IPv6)
  src/netif/ethernet.c            the Ethernet layer
  src/include/lwip, .../netif     the headers (without the apps and PPP headers)

Added for QEMU:

  port/lwipopts.h                 the compile-time options (NO_SYS, raw API, pools)
  port/arch/cc.h                  the platform definitions
  meson.build                     builds a static library and provides the dependency 'lwip'

lwIP is configured at compile time (lwipopts.h decides the layout of its
structures), so it is built with QEMU's options instead of using a system
library. The user is hw/s390x/iucv-tcpip.c, the IUCV TCP/IP service, which
runs the stack in QEMU's main loop.

To update: copy the same files from a newer release, keep port/ and meson.build,
and adjust the commit above.
